**************** CORNERS OF CAPACITORS (ihp-sg13cmos5l) ****************
* The only capacitor in cmos5l is the interdigitated MoM cap_cmomi (the MIM
* caps cmim/rfcmim need the forbidden MIM layer and are excluded).  cap_cmomi
* is an OSDI compact model; the 2-terminal wrapper subckt lives in cap_cmomi.lib
* and the OSDI object auto-loads via libs.tech/ngspice/.spiceinit.
*
* NOTE (caveat, see cap_cmomi.lib / the Verilog-A header): cap_cmomi has NO
* characterised process-corner or mismatch spread yet -- the coefficients are the
* g2-derived NOMINAL values, transferred to cmos5l by layer count and not
* validated on cmos5l silicon.  So EVERY corner/mismatch/stat section below maps
* to the SAME nominal model.  This is not a claim of corner-stability; the spread
* is simply not modelled (pending silicon).  The section names mirror g2's
* cornerCAP.lib so a corner sweep written against g2 resolves unchanged.
***********************************************************************

* Typical without statistical modeling
.LIB cap_typ
.include cap_cmomi.lib
.ENDL cap_typ

* Typical with mismatch modeling (nominal: no characterised mismatch)
.LIB cap_typ_mismatch
.include cap_cmomi.lib
.ENDL cap_typ_mismatch

* Typical with statistical modeling (nominal: no characterised spread)
.LIB cap_typ_stat
.include cap_cmomi.lib
.ENDL cap_typ_stat

* Best Case without statistical modeling (nominal)
.LIB cap_bcs
.include cap_cmomi.lib
.ENDL cap_bcs

* Best Case with mismatch modeling (nominal)
.LIB cap_bcs_mismatch
.include cap_cmomi.lib
.ENDL cap_bcs_mismatch

* Worst Case without statistical modeling (nominal)
.LIB cap_wcs
.include cap_cmomi.lib
.ENDL cap_wcs

* Worst Case with mismatch modeling (nominal)
.LIB cap_wcs_mismatch
.include cap_cmomi.lib
.ENDL cap_wcs_mismatch
